sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch14-10--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch14-10: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.26";
    dc:description "The convergence of those fractions to the golden mean is mathematics, and the further assertion that the convergence has no biological significance is an interpretation of that mathematics. Phyllotactic counts are compatible with the coincidence reading and with models in which the golden angle is an attractor of growth. No dataset outcome decides which reading is the significant one without an extra definition the claim does not supply.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: The continued-fraction limit of 1/2, 2/3, 3/5, … is an arithmetic fact about those fractions. Calling the limit biologically insignificant, and the precise divergence unimportant, does not state a measurement that would separate a coincidence from a developmental attractor, because both accounts produce the same sequence.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "A packing optimum, a dynamical attractor, and a mathematical coincidence can leave identical parastichy counts.", "Biological significance is not defined as a variable or a decision threshold.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.7"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.258"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "not-empirically-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch14-10--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of thompson1917-ch14-10 by Grok 4.7: 0.35";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/analysis-feasibility";
